Call the lock-selected distributions directly (duckdb, sqlite3, pyarrow, psycopg 3, mysql-connector-python, pyodbc, google-cloud-bigquery, trino, databricks-sql-connector, databricks-sdk, adbc_driver_manager and the adbc_driver_flightsql/postgresql/snowflake/sqlite/duckdb/chdb packages, chdb, cassandra-driver, nebula3-python, boto3, prompt_toolkit, pygments, questionary, shandy-sqlfmt (import sqlfmt.api and sqlfmt.mode), pyperclip, tomlkit, platformdirs, rich, wcwidth, babel, filelock); no Cott facade or binding wraps them. Other harlequin callables are reached only through their public generated facades (from real.harlequin.<module> import <name>).
Implementations may not define classes, nested functions, decorators, global/nonlocal statements or mutable module globals: keep state that callbacks change in local one-element lists or dicts (cells) created by the canonical function and pass them to top-level private helpers with lambdas that CALL such helpers by exact name: kb.add(*keys)(lambda event: _handler(cells, event)). Never pass a helper name as a bare value or to functools.partial; the implementation audit rejects helper references except as exact calls. Avoid getattr, hasattr, setattr and other reflection. Do not assign an imported Cott callable to a variable, pass it as a value, or call it through a callback alias. Call app.invalidate() directly rather than assigning it to a local callback name.
A prompt_toolkit completer without subclassing is typing.cast(prompt_toolkit.completion.Completer, types.SimpleNamespace(get_completions=lambda document, complete_event: _complete(cells, document, complete_event), get_completions_async=...)) wrapped in prompt_toolkit.completion.ThreadedCompleter; ThreadedCompleter only calls get_completions(document, complete_event) on the wrapped object. FormattedTextControl takes a callable returning a list of (style, text) tuples; Window(content=..., height=D(weight=1)) sizes panes; ConditionalContainer(content, filter=Condition(lambda: _pred(cells))) hides panes; Float/FloatContainer hosts dialogs and notifications.
Background work runs on threading.Thread(target=lambda: _worker(cells, app), daemon=True): workers change cells under a threading.Lock stored in the cells and then call app.invalidate(), which prompt_toolkit accepts from any thread; blocking database calls never run on the event loop thread.
Untyped or partly typed distributions (boto3, botocore, cassandra-driver, nebula3-python, pyodbc results, trino, databricks, pyperclip, questionary answers, sqlfmt): bind the module or object to a name annotated typing.Any (for example sdk: Any = boto3) and convert every value read from it with cast(object, ...) followed by isinstance checks, or str()/int()/bool() of a narrowed value, before it reaches typed code; never leave Unknown types.
Opaque handles: build them with cott_runtime.Opaque(tag="<the alias tag>", value=obj) and read them with cast(<concrete type>, handle.unwrap()) after checking handle.tag; do not isinstance-test a value already typed Opaque.
BasedPyright narrowing: iterate CottList values directly; narrow Option with isinstance(value, Some) and treat the else branch as Nothing; handle the last variant of a closed enum union in a final else without another isinstance test; do not isinstance-test a value whose static type already guarantees it; do not cast an expression already typed object.
After isinstance(raw, dict) or isinstance(raw, list), cast to dict[str, object] or list[object] before keys, indexing, iteration or assignment, then validate each member; json.loads and tomlkit values are handled the same way.
psycopg typing: build conninfo with psycopg.conninfo.make_conninfo and pass it positionally to psycopg.connect; pass user SQL to Cursor.execute as UTF-8 bytes; fixed SQL stays LiteralString; psycopg connections are psycopg.Connection[tuple[object, ...]]. isinstance(value, memoryview) yields memoryview[Unknown]: cast(memoryview[int], value) before bytes(value).
pyarrow is partly typed: bind pyarrow modules used for construction or writing (pyarrow, pyarrow.csv, pyarrow.json, pyarrow.parquet, pyarrow.orc, pyarrow.feather, pyarrow.ipc) to names annotated typing.Any and convert what they return with cast(object, ...) plus checks; a ResultSet's data payload is exactly a pyarrow.Table.
subprocess typing: annotate text-mode processes as subprocess.Popen[str] and subprocess.CompletedProcess[str]; stream helper parameters are typing.IO[str].
Error helpers return the declared error union type (for example Err[<ErrorEnum>]), not a variant-specific Err. Path values are pathlib.Path. Composition roots declared -> Never keep the exact signature def <name>(arguments: CottList[str]) -> Never with Never from typing and end every path in sys.exit(status).
cott-domain real.harlequin.results.selection_text return: At the partly typed pyarrow boundary, use explicit local annotations such as table: Any = handle.unwrap() and selected: Any = table.select(...), then narrow the returned cells before typed formatting. Do not wrap an expression already typed Any in cast(Any, ...): the pinned checker rejects that redundant cast. This is typing guidance, not permission to weaken the formal output contract.
cott-domain real.harlequin.export.write_result return: Create each short-lived DuckDB export connection with duckdb.connect(config={"threads": 1}) and use that connection for from_arrow, COPY and writer relations. Native defaults size the worker pool from host CPU count and can abort when a bounded process/thread budget is reached; the single-thread setting preserves export content without changing sandbox limits. Do not use the module-global DuckDB connection for export.
cott-domain real.harlequin.app.build_ide return: Every lambda with parameters must first be assigned to a local annotated Callable with explicit argument and return types, including KeyPressEvent handlers and notify, open_dialog and focus callbacks stored in the object-valued state dictionary. Passing a lambda directly to kb.add(...), casting its resulting value to object, or placing it directly in dict[str, object] does not supply parameter types to BasedPyright. Pass the typed local callback, whose lambda body directly calls the private helper; do not pass the helper itself. Remove unused imports.
cott-domain real.harlequin.adapters.connect return: At this callable's logical database-operation boundary, invoke cott_runtime._cott_fixture_database("connect") exactly once inside the existing driver-error handler, before the actual SDK operation. The connect boundary includes its setup queries; do not count internal SDK substeps as additional boundaries. Ignore only the exact inactive-adapter violation outside scenarios; map active injected OSError to the declared operation error, preserve genuine SDK handles, and continue real SDK work when no failure is injected.
cott-domain real.harlequin.adapters.execute_statements return: Invoke cott_runtime._cott_fixture_database("write") exactly once inside normal driver-error handling before the logical statement batch; do not count SDK substeps separately. Ignore only the exact inactive-adapter violation outside scenarios and otherwise map injected errors as declared. Retain each successfully returned PendingResult's actual cursor/relation in the same session's active list until fetch_result closes and removes it; do not remove or close the produced cursor while returning it. Clean up only failed or non-result cursors. This preserves the existing documented connection ownership and fetch lifecycle, without fabricated handles.
